  "strategy": "\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Approach and Rationale:\nThe Triangle Multiplicative Update Outgoing (TriMulOut) kernel is implemented using Triton's capabilities for fusion and spatial transformation. The key bottleneck is the O(N^3) operation in the core update, which is optimized by:\n1. Performing LayerNorm within fp16 precision for memory and computation benefits\n2. Projecting the input tensor through two linear layers to hidden dimension (h)\n3. Applying optional sequence-level masking using fp16 weights\n4. Computing three sigmoid gating functions (left_gate, right_gate, out_gate)\n5. Reducing the core operation to a single blocked matrix multiplication (MM) using Triton's layout optimization\n\nerrorMsg",
